  "id": "object-of-consciousness",
  "term": "object of consciousness",
  "definition": "In this historical usage, the object of consciousness is what the mind is aware of or directed toward at a given moment. In a unified act of knowing or pursuing an end, it is the same object that may be only partly specified at first and becomes more fully defined as consciousness develops.",
